# port scratch space
scratch/

# local build config
.env.local
.env

# Local throwaway Postgres for the server suites.
#
# It normally lives outside the repo, at %LOCALAPPDATA%\360-peoplehub-pg — it used
# to sit under AppData\Local\Temp, which Windows cleanup purged mid-session and
# destroyed. These entries are a guard for anyone who points it at the working
# tree instead: a cluster's data directory must never be stageable.
.data/
pgtest/

# Every dotenv variant, not just .env and .env.local.
.env.*
!.env.example

# Database dumps. A backup of this database contains every employee's personal
# data, so it must never be committed. Root-anchored, so migrations under
# server/db/migrations stay tracked.
#
# The runbook writes backups outside the repo entirely — the repo lives in
# OneDrive, so a dump written anywhere inside it is also synced to the cloud.
# These rules are the second line of defence, not the first.
/backup-*.sql
/backup-*.sql.gz
/*.dump
/pg_dump-*.sql
